+## Usage across tool rounds
+
+`afterModelResponse` is called once per user message, after the round loop exits, and its `usage` argument covers the whole turn rather than its final provider call (re-cinq/HALEngine#93).
+
+- For a turn that ran tool rounds, `usage` is the field-by-field sum of the usage every provider call in that turn reported ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call in a turn that ran two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L64)).
+- A round whose provider reported no usage adds nothing to the sum and does not make it `undefined` or `NaN`; a turn in which no round reported usage passes `undefined` ([validated by: counts the rounds that reported usage, and reports none when no round reported any](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L74)).
+- A turn that called no tools reports exactly its single provider call's usage, as before ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
